// @id 01M4RYJQMNPC71F29BSCJRSSFA
q: In geometry, a ==secant== is a line that intersects a curve at a minimum of two distinct points.
e: [image:media/circle-lines.svg]

// @id 01M4RYJQMNP3D107A85V3XS1AX
q: A ==tangent line== is the straight line that touches a curve at exactly one point and has the same slope as the curve at that point.
e: [image:media/circle-lines.svg]
